<p class="copy">
	Cutters are a broad category of small, utilitarian civilian starships. Built with the minimum necessary aether sails and a fuel gate, these catchall vessels are the economic backbone of the Settled Systems, providing everything from personal transport and delivery to inspection and catering services. There is no standard shape to a cutter, with its form almost always matching its function. A cutter operated as a mobile repair vessel may feature external manipulator arms and heavy cutting equipment, while one run as a luxury taxi might boast overbuilt engines for speed, giving over most of its internal volume to a plush cabin and sleeping space.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	If a cutter is armed at all, it’s often little more than a weak point-defense laser or light autocannon. Enough to deal with debris or an aggressive <?php echo sf_lore_link('skiffs', 'skiff'); ?>, but not much else. Cutters are, by far, the most common hull type for pirate vessels. Indeed, many are little more than civilian cutters with the registration removed.
</p>
